@682280 We'll take a look into this for you. Which device are you encountering this issue on? @682280 Let's try to isolate this a little by swapping out cords to see if the issue is with the aux cord or the iPhone itself. Do you have a different aux cord you can try? Are you able to hear music through earphones? @682280 Just so we understand the issue:
- Is your friend using a different aux cord with her iPhone in her car?
- Are you referring to a cord that connects to the Lightning to Audio Adapter, and then connects to the Aux port on your car, for a direct connection? @682280 Let's look into that further. Send us a DM and we'll go from there. https://t.co/GDrqU22YpT

@656923 Hey there, we're happy to help! 

Are you using Control Center to disconnect from Wi-Fi? @656923 Got it. When you use Control Center to disconnect Wi-Fi, your device will immediately disconnect from any connected Wi-Fi networks, but the Wi-Fi remains active. 

If you want to completely disable Wi-Fi, go to Settings &gt; Wi-Fi and turn off Wi-Fi. @656923 You're welcome. Have a great day!
